olmström J (2023) Democratizing artificial intelligence: how no-code AI can leverage machine learning operations. Bus Horiz 66:777–788 10.1016/j.bushor.2023.04.003 [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 42. Ruamviboonsuk P, Chantra S, Seresirikachorn K et al (2021) Economic evaluations of artificial intelligence in ophthalmology. Asia Pac J Ophthalmol (Phila) 10:307–316 10.1097/APO.0000000000000403 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 43. Gomez Rossi J, Rojas-Perilla N, Krois J, Schwendicke F (2022) Cost-effectiveness of artificial intelligence as a decision-support system applied to the detection and grading of melanoma, dental caries, and diabetic retinopathy. JAMA Netw Open 5:e220269 10.1001/jamanetworkopen.2022.0269 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 44. Subbiah V (2023) The next generation of evidence-based medicine. Nat Med 29:49–58 10.1038/s41591-022-02160-z [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 45. Seebock P, Orlando JI, Schlegl T et al (2020) Exploiting epistemic uncertainty of anatomy segmentation for anomaly detection in retinal OCT. IEEE Trans Med Imaging 39:87–98 10.1109/TMI.2019.2919951 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 46. Nguyen QH, Ly H-B, Ho LS et al (2021) Influence of data splitting on performance of machine learning models in prediction of shear strength of soil. Math Probl Eng 2021. 10.1155/2021/4832864 47. Althnian A, AlSaeed D, Al-Baity H et al (2021) Impact of dataset size on classification performance: an empirical evaluation in the medical domain. NATO Adv Sci Inst Ser E Appl Sci 11:796 [ Google Scholar ] 48. Ahuja AS, Wagner IV, Dorairaj S et al (2022) Artificial intelligence in ophthalmology: a multidisciplinary approach. Integr Med Res 11:100888 10.1016/j.imr.2022.100888 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 49. Lai TYY, Wong VWY, Leung GM (2003) Is ophthalmology evidence based? A clinical audit of the emergency unit of a regional eye hospital. Br J Ophthalmol 87:385–390 10.1136/bjo.87.4.385 [ DOI ]