ialty choice and career plans of Wisconsin''s medical students. WMJ. 2008;107:369–73. [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 12. Khater-Menassa B, Major S. Factors influencing the choice of specialty among medical students in Lebanon. J Med Liban. 2005;53:16–20. [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 13. Johnson AL, Sharma J, Chinchilli VM, Emery SE, McCollister Evarts C, Floyd MW, et al. Why do medical students choose orthopaedics as a career? J Bone Joint Surg Am. 2012;94:e78. doi: 10.2106/JBJS.K.00826. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 14. Elzain YI, Alawad AA, Khan WS, Khalil HO, Abdelrazig YM, Ahmed OB, et al. Factors influencing the choice of internal medicine as a career among undergraduate medical students. Int J Health. 2014;2:22–5. [ Google Scholar ] 15. Saigal P, Takemura Y, Nishiue T, Fetters MD. Factors considered by medical students when formulating their specialty preferences in Japan: Findings from a qualitative study. BMC Med Educ. 2007;7:31. doi: 10.1186/1472-6920-7-31. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 16. Takeda Y, Morio K, Snell L, Otaki J, Takahashi M, Kai I, et al. Characteristic profiles among students and junior doctors with specific career preferences. BMC Med Educ. 2013;13:125. doi: 10.1186/1472-6920-13-125. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 17. Aydin S, Yaris F, Sahin ME, Ozer C, Ozkomur E. Students''perceptions of their undergraduate medical education. Saudi Med J. 2005;26:1484–6. [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 18. Khader Y, Al-Zoubi D, Amarin Z, Alkafagei A, Khasawneh M, Burgan S, et al. Factors affecting medical students in formulating their specialty preferences in Jordan. BMC Med Educ. 2008;8:32. doi: 10.1186/1472-6920-8-32. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 19. Mehmood SI, Kumar A, Al-Binali A, Borleffs JC. Specialty preferences: Trends and perceptions among Saudi undergraduate medical students. Med Teach. 2012;34(Suppl 1):S51–60. doi: 10.3109/0142159X.2012.656753. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 20. Abdulghani HM, Al-Shaikh G, Alhujayri AK, Alohaideb NS, Alsaeed HA, Alshohayeb IS, et al. What determines the selection of undergraduate medical students to the specialty of their future careers? Med Teach. 2013;35(Suppl 1):S25–30. doi: 10.3109/0142159X.2013.765548. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 21. Iftikhar R, Alkhail BA, Alkhail YB, Alkhail MB. More internists, family physicians, and paediatricians and less obstetricians/gynaecologists: Challenges to the workforce. Life Sci J. 2015:12. [ Google Scholar ] 22. Savur SA. Chasing a postgraduate degree in ophthalmology: The medical intern''s perspective. J Clin Diagn Res. 2012:6. [ Google Scholar ] 23. Kaliyadan F, Amin TT, Qureshi H, Al Wadani F. Specialty preferences of 1st year medical students in a Saudi medical school – Factors affecting these choices and the influence of gender. Avicenna J Med. 2015;5:134–9. doi: 10.4103/2231-0770.165120. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 24. Alwadani F, Alrushood A, Altokhy H, Alasbali T. A forecast of ophthalmology practice trends in Saudi Arabia: A survey of junior residents. Middle East Afr J Ophthalmol. 2010;17:343–8. doi: 10.4103/0974-9233.71606. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 25. Nallala S, Swain S, Das S, Kasam SK, Pati S. Why medical students do not like to join rural health service? An exploratory study in India. J Family Community Med. 2015;22:111–7. doi: 10.4103/2230-8229.155390. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ]',25,'2025-10-14 09:53:38','2025-10-14 09:53:38');
