 [ Google Scholar ] 33. Olivier MMG, Forster S, Carter KD, Cruz OA, Lee PP. Lighting a pathway: the Minority Ophthalmology Mentoring program. Ophthalmology. 2020;127(7):848-851. doi: 10.1016/j.ophtha.2020.02.021 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 34. Frierson HT Jr. Black medical students’ perceptions of the academic environment and of faculty and peer interactions. J Natl Med Assoc. 1987;79(7):737-743. [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 35. Sedlacek WE, Prieto DO. Predicting minority students’ success in medical school. Acad Med. 1990;65(3):161-166. doi: 10.1097/00001888-199003000-00007 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 36. Dickins K, Levinson D, Smith SG, Humphrey HJ. The minority student voice at one medical school: lessons for all? Acad Med. 2013;88(1):73-79. doi: 10.1097/ACM.0b013e3182769513 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 37. Elhusseiny AM, Oke I, Adomfeh J, Chauhan MZ, VanderVeen DK. Association of neighborhood environment with the outcomes of childhood glaucoma. Ophthalmol Glaucoma. Published online June 10, 2023. doi: 10.1016/j.ogla.2023.06.001 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 38. Chauhan MZ, Elhusseiny AM, Rook BS, et al. Socioeconomic and racial disparities in vision care access and impairment among United States children. Ophthalmology. 2023;130(7):772-775. doi: 10.1016/j.ophtha.2023.02.019 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 39. Boatright D, Berg D, Genao I. A roadmap for diversity in medicine during the age of COVID-19 and George Floyd. J Gen Intern Med. 2021;36(4):1089-1091. doi: 10.1007/s11606-020-06430-9 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 40. Montgomery Rice V. Diversity in medical schools: a much-needed new beginning. JAMA. 2021;325(1):23-24. doi: 10.1001/jama.2020.21576 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Associated Data This section collects any data citations, data availability statements, or supplementary materials included in this article. Supplementary Materials Supplement. Data Sh